# Wasp moves from custom DSL to TypeScript spec and rebrands in Launch Week #12
created: 2026-07-21, last updated: 2026-07-21, [Read more](https://reasoncore.dev/post/wasp-moves-from-custom-dsl-to-typescript-spec-and-rebrands-in-launch-week-12)

The canonical imports are provided from the @wasp.sh/spec package.
The canonical import line shown in the docs is:
```
import { app, page, query, route } from "@wasp.sh/spec"
```
The official example from the TS Spec materials demonstrates the new pattern and usage (verbatim):
```
// main.wasp.ts
import { app, page, query, route } from "@wasp.sh/spec";
import { MainPage } from "./src/MainPage" with { type: "ref" };
import { getTasks } from "./src/queries" with { type: "ref" };
import { paymentsSpec } from "./src/payments/payments.wasp";
export default app({
name: "TodoApp",
wasp: { version: "^0.24.0" },
auth: {
userEntity: "User",
methods: { google: {}, gitHub: {}, email: {} },
},
spec: [
route("RootRoute", "/", page(MainPage, { authRequired: true })),
query(getTasks, { entities: ["Task"] }),
...paymentsSpec, // <- split your spec across files
],
});
```

